course: dictionary
lesson: 11126
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, read the words around it. These are its context, and they leave clues. «Whoop» can mean a shout of joy, a cough sound, or beating someone easily, so the sentence must tell you which.
explain: «Toad puffed up to twice his size, whooping» shows Toad is excited and loud. Whoop here means to shout loudly with joy. Check by swapping in your meaning: does the sentence still make sense? It does.
explain: In health lessons, whooping cough is an illness, and babies have vaccines against it. Whoops, with an s, is a different little word, said after a small mistake. Look at the clues before you decide.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: A word can have several meanings, and the context shows which one is meant.
fact: «Whoop» can mean to shout loudly with joy or excitement.
fact: Whooping cough is a disease that babies are vaccinated against.
fact: «Whoops» (with s) is a small word said after a little mistake, not the same as whoop.
exercise: Lily reads: «The babies had their vaccines against whooping cough.» Whooping cough is what? | *An illness | A party game | A loud cheer at a football match | A type of cake
exercise: «Toad puffed up to twice his size, whooping» means Toad was doing what? | Falling asleep | Beating everyone at a game | *Shouting loudly with joy | Coughing badly
exercise: Which word is said after a small mistake, like dropping a cup? | *Whoops | Whoop | Whooping cough | Whoop it up
test: «Spotted hyenas use whoops and giggles to talk.» What is a hyena's whoop used for? | *To call the clan | To show it is clean | To hide from lions | To catch food
test: What does the phrase «whoop it up» mean? | To count to ten | To fall over | To cough loudly | *To party noisily
exam: Mo reads «Toad puffed up to twice his size, whooping» and asks what whooping shows. | Toad is ill with a cough | Toad is making a small mistake | Toad is very tired | *Toad is excited and shouting loudly
